      "llm": {
        "status": "verified",
        "verified_on": "2026-09-29",
        "verified_version": "opencode 1.18.32",
        "binary": "opencode",
        "argv": [
          "opencode",
          "run",
          "--pure",
          "--agent",
          "simplicio-planner",
          "--format",
          "json",
          "--title",
          "simplicio-turbo"
        ],
        "model_args": [
          "-m",
          "{model}"
        ],
        "prompt": "stdin",
        "system": "agent",
        "setup": "opencode",
        "env": {
          "OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG": "1",
          "OPENCODE_PERMISSION": "{\"*\":\"deny\"}"
        },
        "output": "jsonl",
        "parse": "opencode",
        "fatal_stderr": [
          "not found\\. Falling back to default agent"
        ],
        "network": "allowed",
        "tools": "disabled",
        "cost": "catalog-estimate",
        "overhead_tokens": 220,
        "notes": "Runs on the user's own OpenCode configuration, provider and default model; one planner agent (no tools, no model) is merged in through OPENCODE_CONFIG and nothing is written to the user's config. A missing agent falls back to the tool-enabled default agent, so tools are also denied through OPENCODE_PERMISSION, and the project's AGENTS.md is kept out of the call (OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG). Sessions go to a scratch OPENCODE_DB under .simplicio-loop/host-llm/. Reasoning is switched off only for openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash. A dead network makes opencode retry for about a minute before it fails; the connect probe catches that first."
      }
